the baryons, and the red line is their MOND fit.</figcaption></figure>
<p>This is terrible! The MOND fit =E2=80=93 essentially a parameter-free pr=
ediction =E2=80=93 misses all of the data. MOND is falsified. If one is inc=
lined to hate MOND, as many seem to be, then one stops here. No need to thi=
nk further.</p>
<p>If one is familiar with the ups and downs in the history of astronomy, o=
ne might not be so quick to dismiss it. Indeed, one might notice that the s=
hape of the MOND prediction closely tracks the shape of the data. There=E2=
=80=99s just a little difference in scale. That=E2=80=99s kind of amazing f=
or a theory that is wrong, especially when it is amplifying the green line =
to predict the red one: it needn=E2=80=99t have come anywhere close.</p>
<p>Here is the fit to the same galaxy using the same data [already] publish=
ed in <a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.00553" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D=
"noopener">Li et al.</a>:</p>
<figure data-shortcode=3D"caption" id=3D"attachment_7053" aria-describedby=
=3D"caption-attachment-7053" style=3D"width: 411px" class=3D"wp-caption ali=
gncenter fix-link-focus"><img data-attachment-id=3D"7053" data-permalink=3D=
"https://tritonstation.com/2018/11/21/hypothesis-testing-with-gas-rich-gala=
xies/ddo154_rar_li2018/" data-orig-file=3D"https://tritonstation.files.word=
press.com/2018/11/ddo154_rar_li2018.png" data-orig-size=3D"411,298" data-co=
mments-opened=3D"1" data-image-meta=3D"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,=
