154 from Li et al. (2018) using the same data as above, as tabulated in <a =
href=3D"http://astroweb.case.edu/SPARC/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener"=
>SPARC</a>.</figcaption></figure>
<p>Now we have a good fit, using the same data! How can this be so?</p>
<p>I have not checked what <a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.05695" tar=
get=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener">Ren et al</a>. did to obtain their MOND fit=
s, but having done this exercise myself many times, I recognize the slight =
offset they find as a typical consequence of holding the nuisance parameter=
s fixed. What if the measured distance is a little off?</p>
<p><a href=3D"http://ned.ipac.caltech.edu/?q=3Dbyname&amp;omegam=3D0.27&amp=
;corr_z=3D1&amp;extend=3Dno&amp;img_stamp=3DYES&amp;out_csys=3DEquatorial&a=
mp;objname=3DDDO%20154&amp;list_limit=3D5&amp;omegav=3D0.73&amp;of=3Dpre_te=
xt&amp;obj_sort=3DRA%20or%20Longitude&amp;out_equinox=3DJ2000.0&amp;hconst=
=3D73" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener">Distance estimates</a> to DDO 154=
 in the literature range from 3.02 Mpc to 6.17 Mpc. The formally most accur=
ate distance measurement is 4.04 =C2=B1 0.08 Mpc. In the fit shown here, we=
 obtained 3.87 =C2=B1 0.16 Mpc. The error bars on these distances overlap, =
so they are the same number, to measurement accuracy. These data do not fal=
sify MOND. They demonstrate that it is sensitive enough to tell the differe=
nce between 3.8 and 4.1 Mpc.</p>
<p>One will never notice this from a dark matter fit. <a href=3D"https://ar=
xiv.org/abs/1808.05695">Ren et al</a>. also make fits with self-interacting=
 dark matter (SIDM). The nifty thing about SIDM is that it makes quasi-cons=
tant density cores in dark matter halos. Halos of this form are not predict=
ed by =E2=80=9Cordinary=E2=80=9D cold dark matter (CDM), but often give bet=
ter fits than either MOND of the NFW halos of dark matter-only CDM simulati=
ons. For this galaxy, <a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.05695">Ren et a=
l</a>. obtain the following SIDM fit.</p>
<figure data-shortcode=3D"caption" id=3D"attachment_7054" aria-describedby=
=3D"caption-attachment-7054" style=3D"width: 396px" class=3D"wp-caption ali=
gncenter fix-link-focus"><img data-attachment-id=3D"7054" data-permalink=3D=
"https://tritonstation.com/2018/11/21/hypothesis-testing-with-gas-rich-gala=
xies/ddo154_sidm_180805695/" data-orig-file=3D"https://tritonstation.files.=
