<p>Our failure to trick MOND should not surprise anyone who bothers to look=
 at the math involved. There is a one-to-one relation between the distribut=
ion of the baryons and the resulting rotation curve. If there is a mismatch=
 between them, a fit cannot be obtained.</p>
<p>We also attempted to play this same trick on dark matter. The standard d=
ark matter halo fitting function at the time was the pseudo-isothermal halo=
, which has a constant density core. It is very similar to the halos of SID=
M and to the cored dark matter halos produced by baryonic feedback in some =
simulations. Indeed, that is the point of those efforts: they&nbsp; are try=
ing to capture the success of cored dark matter halos in fitting rotation c=
urve data.</p>
